# What must never reach the image.
#
# The first entry is the one that matters: .env holds the service-role key,
# which bypasses row-level security on every table. An image is a tarball
# anyone who can pull it can read, so a baked .env is a published master key.
# Secrets are injected at run time instead (see the Dockerfile header).
.env
*.env

# 1.7GB of cover frames and the scraped corpus. Nothing in the worker reads
# these, and copying them makes every build slow for no reason.
output/
data/

# macOS-only virtualenv — wrong platform, wrong interpreter, and it would
# shadow the packages pip installs in the image.
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The site. The worker writes scripts; it does not serve pages.
*.html
*.css
*.js
agencyonly/
creatorsonly/
privacy/
fonts/
*.png
*.ico
*.svg

# Repo furniture
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
*.md
supabase/
.DS_Store
